    <briefdescription>
<para>The id types, and nothing that costs anything to include. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Most headers that name something from ecss name only an id: a component recording which entity owns it, a system interface taking a list of entities to process, a renderer keying a cache. None of them touch a Registry, and none of them should pay for one.</para>
<para><ref refid="Types_8h_source" kindref="compound">Types.h</ref> cannot be that header. It carries the sector offset arithmetic, which wants &lt;array&gt; and &lt;tuple&gt;, and the seqlock helpers, which want &lt;atomic&gt; and (on MSVC) &lt;intrin.h&gt;. That came to 55k preprocessed lines for a caller that wanted a uint32_t.</para>
<para>Include this when an id is all that is needed; <ref refid="Types_8h_source" kindref="compound">Types.h</ref> pulls it in, so everything that already includes <ref refid="Types_8h_source" kindref="compound">Types.h</ref> is unaffected. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
